he function returns `False` if fewer than three inputs are provided.\\n   - Ensure the function returns `False` if more than three inputs are provided.\\n\\n7. **Edge Cases**\\n   - Test with zero and negative integers to ensure they are handled correctly.\\n\\n8. **Complexity**\\n   - Ensure the function has a time complexity of O(1) and a space complexity of O(1).\\n\\n### Example Implementations\\n\\n```python\\ndef any_int(x, y, z):\\n    # Check if exactly three inputs are provided\\n    if len([x, y, z]) != 3:\\n        return False\\n    \\n    # Check if all inputs are integers\\n    if not all(isinstance(i, int) for i in [x, y, z]):\\n        return False\\n    \\n    # Check if any one of the numbers is equal to the sum of the other two\\n    if x == y + z or y == x + z or z == x + y:\\n        return True\\n    \\n    # If none of the above conditions are met, return False\\n    return False\\n```\\n\\nThis checklist ensures that the function `any_int(x, y, z)` is implemented correctly according to the given specification."}'}]
